concepts.content:
A fully connected layer (fc layer) over tokens is defined as a mapping from $N_1$ input tokens to $N_2$ output tokens. It is parameterized by a matrix $\mathbf{W} \in \mathbb{R}^{N_2 \times N_1}$ and optionally by a set of token biases $\mathbf{b} \in \mathbb{R}^{N_2 \times d}$:

$$\begin{aligned}
    \mathbf{T}_{\texttt{out}}&= \mathbf{W}\mathbf{T}_{\texttt{in}}+ \mathbf{b} \quad\quad &\triangleleft \quad \text{fc layer over tokens}
\end{aligned}$$

