concepts.content:
To compute the query, key, and value for a set of input tokens, $\mathbf{T}_{\texttt{in}}$, we apply the same linear transformations to each token in the set, resulting in matrices $\mathbf{Q}_{\texttt{in}}, \mathbf{K}_{\texttt{in}} \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times m}$ and $\mathbf{V}_{\texttt{in}} \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times d}$, where each row is the query/key/value for each token. Note that the query and key vectors must have the same dimensionality, $m$, because we take a dot product between them. Conversely, the value vectors must match the dimensionality of the token code vectors, $d$, because these are summed up to produce the new token code vectors.

$$\begin{aligned}
    \mathbf{Q}_{\texttt{in}}&= \mathbf{T}_{\texttt{in}}\mathbf{W}_q^\mathsf{T}&\triangleleft \quad\quad \text{query matrix} \\
    \mathbf{K}_{\texttt{in}}&= \mathbf{T}_{\texttt{in}}\mathbf{W}_k^\mathsf{T}&\triangleleft \quad\quad \text{key matrix}\\
    \mathbf{V}_{\texttt{in}}&= \mathbf{T}_{\texttt{in}}\mathbf{W}_v^\mathsf{T}&\triangleleft \quad\quad \text{value matrix}
\end{aligned}$$

Finally, we have the attention equation:

$$\begin{aligned}
    \mathbf{A} &= f(\mathbf{T}_{\texttt{in}}) = \texttt{softmax}\Big(\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{\texttt{in}}\mathbf{K}_{\texttt{in}}^\mathsf{T}}{\sqrt{m}}\Big) &\triangleleft \quad\quad \text{attention matrix}\\
    \mathbf{T}_{\texttt{out}}&= \mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}_{\texttt{in}}
\end{aligned}$$

